// Corpus fixture for a `[bool]` field in the FlatBuffers codec
// (driftsys/ridl#518).
//
// `flatbuffers_roundtrip.ridl`'s only boolean field, `Engaged`, is an inline
// scalar, not a vector, so the codec's inline-scalar encode path
// (`Field::Bool(value)`) is the only one it exercises. A vector element goes
// through a different path, one that writes every scalar element's raw bytes
// with `.to_le_bytes()` — a method `bool` does not have. This file isolates
// that path: `values` is a bounded vector of the inline `boolean` primitive.
//
// Kept self-contained, in the shape of `flatbuffers_roundtrip.ridl`: no
// cross-package import, one declaration carrying the shape under test.

package fb.boolvec

struct Flags {
  values : [boolean; 0..4]
}
